=== SIGNATURE ===
ad_col_n(ad_or_rng)

=== COMMENT ===
Column number(s) of an address or range. A single address - numeric (66000045) or A1 ("AA99") - becomes its column number; a bare column letter "A".."XFD" ("BDS") becomes its column number even though it has no row; a range string ("B8:D11") becomes a vertical array of the columns it spans. In an array input each single address or column letter is converted, while ranges and non-addresses pass through unchanged.

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(ad_or_rng,
  LET(
    letters_to_col, LAMBDA(one, IFERROR(MOD(z_a1n(one & "1"), 1000000), one)),
    col_of_1, LAMBDA(one,
      LET(box, IFERROR(z_ad_box(one), 0),
        IF(COUNT(box) = 4,
          LET(top, SUM(INDEX(box, 1)), lft, SUM(INDEX(box, 2)),
              bot, SUM(INDEX(box, 3)), rgt, SUM(INDEX(box, 4)),
            IF(AND(top = bot, lft = rgt, top >= 1, lft >= 1), lft, one)),
          letters_to_col(one)))),
    IF(ROWS(ad_or_rng) * COLUMNS(ad_or_rng) > 1,
      MAP(ad_or_rng, col_of_1),
      LET(box, IFERROR(z_ad_box(ad_or_rng), 0),
        IF(COUNT(box) = 4,
          LET(top, SUM(INDEX(box, 1)), lft, SUM(INDEX(box, 2)), rgt, SUM(INDEX(box, 4)),
            IF(AND(top >= 1, lft >= 1),
               IF(lft = rgt, lft, SEQUENCE(rgt - lft + 1, 1, lft)),
               ad_or_rng)),
          letters_to_col(ad_or_rng))))
  )
)

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Column number(s) from an address, range, or bare column letter. The column-wise twin of ad_row_n. Uses the shared z_ad_box parser, so it accepts a numeric address (1e6*row+col, e.g. 66000045), an A1 string ("AA99"), an A1 range ("B8:D11") or a numeric range - plus a bare column-letter string.

Behaviour depends on the input:
  scalar single address        -> its column number         (66000045 -> 45, "AA99" -> 27)
  scalar column letter A..XFD  -> its column number         ("BDS" -> 1475)
  scalar range                 -> a VERTICAL array of the columns it spans   ("B8:D11" -> {2;3;4})
  scalar non-address           -> returned unchanged
  array of values (element-wise):
    each single address        -> its column number
    each column letter A..XFD  -> its column number
    a range, or any non-address-> returned unchanged (a range is never expanded inside an array)

An address only counts when z_ad_box parses it AND its row and column are both >= 1; a column letter counts when z_a1n accepts letter&"1" (1-3 letters, column <= 16384). Anything else passes straight through.

Arguments:
  ad_or_rng - a single address/range/column letter, or an array of them.

Returns:
  A column number, a vertical array of column numbers (scalar range only), the array of per-element results, or the input unchanged where it is not a single address or column letter.

See also ad_row_n (rows), ad_col_let (number -> letters), ad_to_rc, num_ad.
